{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1539675-the-raksha-not-enemies-of-the-sun","id":1539675,"title":"The Raksha: NOT enemies of the Sun?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2024-08-01T20:46:15-07:00","id":1539675,"title":"The Raksha: NOT enemies of the Sun?","content":"Hello everyone. It's been a while, most of you probably don't remember me. Haven't had a lot to say about Exalted of late, until something just occurred to me.<br /> <br /> I'd like to start this question with a simple premise. Imagine one day, you hear about a horde of soul-eating monsters invading Halta, or Lookshy, or just some village out near the edge of the world. They gild themselves in illusion and fancy, stringing along devotees with sweet nothings and fabulous promises. Once the mortals have let their guard down these creatures then <i>devour their souls</i>. Either all at once or piece by piece, spinning out their Valor and Temperance like cotton candy. Oftentimes-not always, but often-these monsters are violent. Styling themselves as conquerors who MUST slay and enslave and ravish, (for the tale they have defined themselves by demands this of them). But even when they style themselves as playful hucksters or innocuous muses instead, these creatures are fundamentally unable to understand, to empathise with the Creation-born on a level more profound than even demons. Since Time Not these entities have never once demonstrated remorse for doing this. In fact, many hold as a point of ideological contention that <i>dissolving Creation back into chaos is their ideal. </i>There has at least been one organised war by these creatures in service of this goal where these creatures warred with the Exalted; you may remember it, it's the one in which the Scarlet Empress claimed her throne. But there have been others before the great crusade, and there are STILL others long after it. They are, by nature, a demonstrable threat to Creation.<br /> <br /> They're called Raksha.<br /> <br /> My question is this: <b>Why the blazes aren't the Raksha considered Creatures of Darkness? </b>Now, I think I already know the game designers' answer: It would be nice if there was a type of supernatural enemy that was not automatically a Creature of Darkness, nor another Exalt. However, Exalted is a game that likes to explore certain story conceits and use them to explain why the world is the way it is, from the Realm's sociopolitical makeup on the brink of civil war to the organisation of Yu-Shan. And it's just struck me that not once, in any edition of Exalted, have I heard a satisfactory in-universe reason for why the Raksha apparently get a free pass from the Unconquered Sun to continue doing what they do since the Time of Glory.<br /> <br /> I'm asking out of curiosity if I've overlooked one. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26460-organ-boy","name":"Organ Boy","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"63"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-01T22:40:19-07:00","id":1539676,"title":"","content":"In the first two editions, it's mostly to contrast the shifting, transient drama magnets that are shaped Fair Folk from the incomprehensible and hostile alien god-monsters that are the Unshaped. In 3e, it's so that you can stuff fae inside human forms with Dream-Souled Charms and turn them into changelings!<br /> <br /> (Also, Solars tend to not really notice them when they melt away the chaos en masse and change entire lands into Creation, so the nature of the sun might just be to not actually care that much about them as a group. Meanwhile, Abyssal powers have tended to melt fae on contact worse than cold iron, which implies that an inverted Solar nature is required to really hate them as a group just because.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-01T22:47:16-07:00","id":1539678,"title":"","content":"I wonder what\u2019s the description of CoD in Ex3 is, maybe we can infer the IC why fey get exempted using that text.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The no.1 fan of Demetheus. I also draw <a href=\"https://probably-unreliable.tumblr.com/tagged/Jenart\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted</a> things and is looking for commission works ~","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/298-jen","name":"Jen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar298_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-01T22:50:09-07:00","id":1539679,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1539675-the-raksha-not-enemies-of-the-sun?p=1539678#post1539678\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I wonder what\u2019s the description of CoD in Ex3 is, maybe we can infer the IC why fey get exempted using that text.</div> </div> </div> </div>Page 61 of Exalted: Essence, and it doesn't really give an indicator, especially since fae don't come in shaped vs unshaped anymore (unless I'm forgetting something). We probably won't get much of one, either, since fae aren't slated to get a playable splat treatment.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-02T00:33:02-07:00","id":1539682,"title":"","content":"Yeah, so.<br /> <br /> In first edition, IIRC, there's no explanation as to why some things are creatures of darkness and some are not.<br /> <br /> In latter 2nd, the definition of creature of darkness became a specific designation by the Unconquered Sun, and it's fair to ask why he didn't go ahead and designate the shaped Fair Folk as such, but just the unshaped.<br /> <br /> In Ex3 <i>qua</i> Ex3, there isn't, in fact, a concise definition of creature of darkness given anywhere. However, Orichalcum Letters of Marque by implication defines it to mean &quot;residents of Malfeas and the Underworld, Abyssal Exalted and other cursed Chosen&quot;, a list not including the Fair Folk.<br /> <br /> In the first draft of the ExEs definition, creatures of darkness were those so designated by the Unconquered Sun (harking back to latter 2e), including <i>all</i> Fair Folk (logically enough):<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Creatures of darkness are formally designated by the Unconquered Sun. He detests them above all else, deeming them the enemies of Creation. His Exalts excel at many things, but one of their greatest talents is for destroying their patron\u2019s enemies: Fair Folk, demons of all circles, the undead and their masters the Deathlords. The ghosts of the dead cannot even bear the touch of the Sun\u2019s light, though paths back to the Most High\u2019s righteous mercy exist. Abyssals, having sworn fealty to the Deathlords, and Infernals, who draw their might from that of the Yozis, are both considered creatures of darkness; however, despite being classified as undead, Liminals are categorically not. </div> </div> </div>In the final version for ExEs, it is rather a different statement that does not include the Fair Folk at all:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Creatures of darkness are enemies of Creation who shun the light of the Unconquered Sun, wretched beings that stalk through the night or dwell in the shadowed places of the world. The Sun\u2019s Chosen excel at many things, but one of their greatest talents is destroying the enemies of Creation: demons of all circles, the undead, and other dark entities hostile to the world. Abyssals, champions of the undead, and Infernals, who draw their might from the Yozis, are creatures of darkness. Despite being undead, Liminals are not. Some beings may be exempted from this status if their deeds prove they aren\u2019t enemies to Creation or its peoples.\u200b </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/572-verzio","name":"Verzio","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar572_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"380"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-02T06:24:52-07:00","id":1539689,"title":"","content":"Third Edition gives its definition of creatures of darkness in the writeup of Golden Janissary Style: &quot;foes of creation who stalk through the night or dwell in the dark places of the world&quot;. Said to entail demons and the dead by default, but can be narrowed or broadened at Storyteller discretion.<br /> <br /> I think the main reason for the shift is that the original developers wanted to make it more about something that would literally be harmed by the cleansing light of the sun, rather than being on a list of enemies.<br /> <br /> Also out of a desire to differentiate the ways that Exalted can inflict aggravated damage; rather than just giving everybody Holy Keyword Charms and letting them get in on beating up what's on the Sun's shitlist, it's all based in how they could harness the particular properties of their Essence. This actually makes the powers of the Dragon Blooded more naturally suited to inflicting such harm on creatures of the Wyld, between things like channelling the stabilizing patterns of Creation that calcify beings of chaos and being able to invoke the Earth to provide a power of iron.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-02T21:00:30-07:00","id":1539735,"title":"","content":"It\u2019s been a while since I played Exalted but I completely agree with the raksha not being creatures of darkness. The raksha are basically fae. They are chaotic and can also be destructive, but they are not inherently opposed to the Sun\u2019s light the way true creatures of darkness are.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Amethyst is my birthstone. She/they.","edited":{"userid":26996,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26996-amethyst","user":"Amethyst","date":". 08-03-2024, 04:57 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26996-amethyst","name":"Amethyst","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26996_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"873"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-03T04:20:06-07:00","id":1539743,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Verzio</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1539675-the-raksha-not-enemies-of-the-sun?p=1539682#post1539682\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, so.<br /> <br /> In first edition, IIRC, there's no explanation as to why some things are creatures of darkness and some are not.<br /> <br /> In latter 2nd, the definition of creature of darkness became a specific designation by the Unconquered Sun, and it's fair to ask why he didn't go ahead and designate the shaped Fair Folk as such, but just the unshaped.<br /> <br /> In Ex3 <i>qua</i> Ex3, there isn't, in fact, a concise definition of creature of darkness given anywhere. However, Orichalcum Letters of Marque by implication defines it to mean &quot;residents of Malfeas and the Underworld, Abyssal Exalted and other cursed Chosen&quot;, a list not including the Fair Folk.<br /> <br /> In the first draft of the ExEs definition, creatures of darkness were those so designated by the Unconquered Sun (harking back to latter 2e), including <i>all</i> Fair Folk (logically enough):<br /> <br /> <br /> In the final version for ExEs, it is rather a different statement that does not include the Fair Folk at all:</div> </div> </div> </div>Huh, that's...confusing. Well, thanks for this and all the other answers. I'll be honest I came in on 2e so the Sun's motivation to defend Creation informed most of my assumptions about how Holy worked, and the idea of the 2e Sun just randomly giving these asshole little fairies the pass for no particular reason just struck me as odd. The Raksha are, unambiguous, chaotic and a detriment to Creation. I don't like the 3e definition because it sounds more generic like in an MMO or something, I like the idea Holy in Exalted is more of a designation than an objective truth, and under that definition there's absolutely no reason to spare the Raksha that label. But it sounds like my initial assumption that it really is just a game thing to have supernatural enemies that aren't automatically weak to basic Solar attack Charms (and aren't something as hard as a Behemoth or high level god) was right.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26460-organ-boy","name":"Organ Boy","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"63"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-04T04:15:12-07:00","id":1539785,"title":"","content":"My (completely non-canon, of course) take is that Sun just lacks the metaphysical sovereignty over the fae needed to change their status by decree. They may be enemies of Creation, but they are still outside His jurisdiction.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><i>The difference between fiction and reality? Fiction has to make sense.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/434-astralporing","name":"Astralporing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar434_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"296"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-05T13:34:13-07:00","id":1539879,"title":"","content":"I think that the Sun maybe would make a difference, in his eyes, between an honourable sporting (if eternal) foe and someone on his &quot;side&quot; of reality that is a complete wrong un","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/117-solar","name":"Solar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar117_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1267"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-05T20:31:27-07:00","id":1539914,"title":"","content":"They were also kind of on their way out, post-Balorian Crusade. They were caught in an ambush that killed them off in massive numbers, such that they would never threaten Creation as a whole ever again - and to top that off, something new came out of the Wyld in 2e that stalked them as preferred prey (the late-2e introduction of the hannya in the errata), so there was no going back. The raksha are, in a word, fucked, and they can squat on their thumbs or try to get in better with Creation. All in all, not a threat the way that, say, nephwracks are.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-06T07:48:33-07:00","id":1539923,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1539675-the-raksha-not-enemies-of-the-sun?p=1539914#post1539914\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They were also kind of on their way out, post-Balorian Crusade. They were caught in an ambush that killed them off in massive numbers, such that they would never threaten Creation as a whole ever again - and to top that off, something new came out of the Wyld in 2e that stalked them as preferred prey (the late-2e introduction of the hannya in the errata), so there was no going back. The raksha are, in a word, fucked, and they can squat on their thumbs or try to get in better with Creation. All in all, not a threat the way that, say, nephwracks are.</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean, I think the presentation of Third Edition has it that there are already forces less powerful than the entire Balorian Crusade who represent a threat to the existence of Creation, especially in aggregate, and something like Spear-Empress Bhadri and her retinue* strikes me as an indication that even in their weakened state even a small number of the mightier raksha can wreak devastation upon the world and its inhabitants.<br /> <br /> Between that and how their work destabilizes reality in a way that many figures in Creation are against as a matter of principle (and which is opposed by the work of destiny and Heaven as a matter of course), I think that if being an enemy to the world at all was sufficient, then they would fall under that definition.<br /> <br /> * Those are a bunch of powerful fae whose onslaught is the driving force behind a sample Lunar Dominion, namely rendering a number of peoples into refugees that have forced them into being a conquering confederation under the leadership of a young Lunar, down in the Southwest.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-10T03:08:52-07:00","id":1540124,"title":"","content":"Do is being CoD a state of existence stemming from a creature\u2019s nature, or something like brand that the Sun gives out? If it\u2019s the former then I guess fey being exempt make sense since nothing about them is exactly \u201cDarkness\u201d, but that would kick demon out of the group either since Hell is 100% full of light OsO","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The no.1 fan of Demetheus. I also draw <a href=\"https://probably-unreliable.tumblr.com/tagged/Jenart\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted</a> things and is looking for commission works ~","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/298-jen","name":"Jen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar298_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-10T06:48:36-07:00","id":1540129,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1539675-the-raksha-not-enemies-of-the-sun?p=1539676#post1539676\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">(Also, Solars tend to not really notice them when they melt away the chaos en masse and change entire lands into Creation, so the nature of the sun might just be to not actually care that much about them as a group. Meanwhile, Abyssal powers have tended to melt fae on contact worse than cold iron, which implies that an inverted Solar nature is required to really hate them as a group just because.)</div> </div> </div> </div>This is where I tend to go. Yeah, some Shaped Raksha hold to an <i>ideology</i> of enmity with Creation, but they are fundamentally creatures of Shape; on a metaphysical level they've &quot;gone native&quot;. From the Sun's perspective that makes <i>Shaped</i> Raksha more akin to human cultists where <i>Unshaped </i>are more like demons.<br /> <br /> Causality itself, managed by the Maidens with help from Luna, results from harnessing the boundless potential energy of the Wyld. That energy is no more inherently inimical to Creation than gasoline is inimical to a car - but at the risk of straining the analogy, the Unshaped are like a Molotov cocktail which. Full of gasoline yes, but NOT friendly to cars.<br /> <br /> But Oblivion is another story. One of those cases where the enemy of my enemy is not necessarily my friend - the Wyld (everything everywhere all at once) and Oblivion (nothing nowhere ever again) are inherently polar opposites; thus the impact Abyssals have on Shaped Raksha.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":456,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/456-blackwell","user":"Blackwell","date":". 08-10-2024, 12:05 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/456-blackwell","name":"Blackwell","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar456_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"977"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-11T14:00:16-07:00","id":1540183,"title":"","content":"They even had that Charm that allowed them to persist in Creation without hurting anyone even without a hearthstone or equivalent!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-12T09:39:00-07:00","id":1540212,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1539675-the-raksha-not-enemies-of-the-sun?p=1540124#post1540124\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do is being CoD a state of existence stemming from a creature\u2019s nature, or something like brand that the Sun gives out? If it\u2019s the former then I guess fey being exempt make sense since nothing about them is exactly \u201cDarkness\u201d, but that would kick demon out of the group either since Hell is 100% full of light OsO</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, the light of Malfeas does differ in some respects to that of the Sun.<br /> <br /> Still, demons as creatures that need to lurk in the night... it's not a strictly literal thing, but I think could still be read in terms of their relationship to the divine order that governs Creation. Still, there is arguably something a bit monstrous and twisted in common to demons.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1539675-the-raksha-not-enemies-of-the-sun?p=1540183#post1540183\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They even had that Charm that allowed them to persist in Creation without hurting anyone even without a hearthstone or equivalent!</div> </div> </div> </div>I think there's a question of whether or not that was a sensible thing for them to have, consistent with the overall presentation. I recall that Holden often expressed unhappiness with anything that really eased the raksha out of needing to be predatory.<br /> <br /> I suppose it's a bit of a moot point when thus far Third Edition makes Fae Nature a Merit that they have in common, defining them specifically as calcifying in Creation unless they feed on mortal souls.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-12T15:13:34-07:00","id":1540226,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1539675-the-raksha-not-enemies-of-the-sun?p=1540212#post1540212\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think there's a question of whether or not that was a sensible thing for them to have, consistent with the overall presentation. I recall that Holden often expressed unhappiness with anything that really eased the raksha out of needing to be predatory.<br /> <br /> I suppose it's a bit of a moot point when thus far Third Edition makes Fae Nature a Merit that they have in common, defining them specifically as calcifying in Creation unless they feed on mortal souls.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>It was phrased as a form of micropredation, and if that's not good enough, Abyssals are going to have to sit on the chair with them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-13T00:14:31-07:00","id":1540265,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1539675-the-raksha-not-enemies-of-the-sun?p=1540226#post1540226\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It was phrased as a form of micropredation</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh wait, did you mean that form of dream eating?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-13T07:50:16-07:00","id":1540272,"title":"","content":"Banquet of Crumbs. Supposedly still brings down the mood of a situation, just not the way affixing a feeding maw to someone does.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-13T17:29:06-07:00","id":1540317,"title":"","content":"I'd say there's a place for something like that if we ever get a more elaborate description of what it means to feed the Fae Nature, although I'd still say it wouldn't exactly be a reassuring thing. A raksha might opt to feed only very lightly for the sake of not creating waves, but I think it would be consistent for that to have a negative effect on their mental state, and possibly create dangers of them becoming erratic and impulsive if more satisfying fare ever presented itself.<br /> <br /> A person in a situation to perform that moral calculus might deem that it's preferable for them to be satiated and relatively stable, at the cost of a somewhat small number of lives, than one that is constantly hungry and on edge and might be provoked into a terrible rampage.<br /> <br /> Still, the idea of being potentially benign is probably not enough to discount being creatures of darkness by itself. Like, some of the less harmful varieties of demon and probably a lot of ghosts fit that criteria and it's not enough to categorically exclude them, while there's still an option for individual good eggs to be excluded anyway.<br /> <br /> Actually, it's occurring to me... wasn't there some sense in Second Edition that shaped raksha weren't Creatures of Darkness primarily because in the era that the Unconquered Sun defended Creation there were hardly any of them and they were largely beneath his notice? I think by the standards of those books, there was also an answer of him not really being in a position to judge them as a threat and add them to the list, whether they warranted being there or not.<br /> <br /> I'm just thinking about that while I'm trying to assess questions of how to reconcile what the power of the Sun is and is not intrinsically anathema to when he's still supposed to have been once the direct guardian of the world. Mind, I suppose that could be resolved by him not exactly needing to inflict aggravated damage on everything he needs to fight off*, or just being able to invoke aggravated damage against everything he attacks by virtue of his sheer overwhelming might.<br /> <br /> Ultimately, it might be a bit of a moot point. You don't really need to have the light of the sun channelled through the strength of his Chosen by the thing to harm them in such fashion when an abundant mundane metal will typically do so.<br /> <br /> * Probably the biggest reason you don't need to inflict aggravated damage on the fae at all is if they don't exactly have much access to healing magic that would give it any distinction from lethal damage in the first place.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-13T19:07:10-07:00","id":1540323,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1539675-the-raksha-not-enemies-of-the-sun?p=1540317#post1540317\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm just thinking about that while I'm trying to assess questions of how to reconcile what the power of the Sun is and is not intrinsically anathema to when he's still supposed to have been once the direct guardian of the world. Mind, I suppose that could be resolved by him not exactly needing to inflict aggravated damage on everything he needs to fight off*, or just being able to invoke aggravated damage against everything he attacks by virtue of his sheer overwhelming might.</div> </div> </div> </div>So a couple of angles to consider.<br /> <br /> Shaped Raksha are a threat to communities of sapient Creation-born, but they're not really a threat to Creation. Unshaped, who I do think are CoD, are actually threatening to Creation; the Sun probably ended them off regularly. And then there are Ishvara; elevated Shaped Raksha. Definitely a threat even to the Sun himself; we have at least two examples of age-of-dreams vintage, Laashe and the Formorian Dream. Would make sense if they were on the list, but maybe the Sun had to put them there by name? Laashe in particular was obsessed with becoming part of the Sun's story; maybe becoming a CoD was a key part of his arc? The Formorian Dream was *definitely* CoD-ish.<br /> <br /> Also, Sol isn't the ONLY guardian of Creation. Hunting Raksha is a big Luna thing. Maybe the Sun focused on the big bad stuff that showed up from time to time, while Luna's hunts thinned out the Raksha. Many Raksha probably resulted from her tides anyway - unshaped stranded when the middlemarches turned to bordermarches fleeing through Sundraprisha?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/456-blackwell","name":"Blackwell","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar456_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"977"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-14T02:24:40-07:00","id":1540334,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Blackwell</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1539675-the-raksha-not-enemies-of-the-sun?p=1540323#post1540323\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Shaped Raksha are a threat to communities of sapient Creation-born, but they're not really a threat to Creation.</div> </div> </div> </div>And hungry ghosts are?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-14T07:16:23-07:00","id":1540352,"title":"","content":"Why aren't siaka creatures of darkness, or tyrant lizards, or giant parasitic wasps, or chakra orchids, the Guild, or those neighboring conquerers who will kill your family and take the survivors as slaves? There are tons of monsters that will kill, or destroy the souls of people while leaving the body alive. The Unconquered Sun doesn't seem to approve of these things, and he exalts those who will defeat such monsters, but they're not creatures of darkness/<br /> <br /> CoD label is reserved for his personal enemies, the fallen primordials and their servants. Why aren't the raksha creatures of darkness, because he didn't fight a divine civil war against them with the other gods and their chosen and reorder the cosmos the lock them away.<br /> <br /> Another angle might be that creatures of darkness are foes who can be defeated (theoretically). Demons and their masters can be locked back in their prison, the neverborn and their arrayed servants can be cast into oblivion and the cosmic order rightened. Raksha emerge from infinity, calling them out as specific enemies of the Sun would be like designating raindrops terrorists. Sure, you could do it, but it doesn't really accomplish anything. Slay an infinity of raksha with your creature of darkness slaying charms and infinity +1 will show up eventually. You don't defeat the rain by targeting individual drops, you build levees and umbrellas and shelters and since it is Exalted you punch the occasional hurricane in the mouth. The Chosen have the tools needed to fight the raksha, and they're not charms that hurt creatures of darkness more.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4270-literatzi","name":"literatzi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4270_2.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-14T17:58:47-07:00","id":1540398,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1539675-the-raksha-not-enemies-of-the-sun?p=1540317#post1540317\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd say there's a place for something like that if we ever get a more elaborate description of what it means to feed the Fae Nature, although I'd still say it wouldn't exactly be a reassuring thing. A raksha might opt to feed only very lightly for the sake of not creating waves, but I think it would be consistent for that to have a negative effect on their mental state, and possibly create dangers of them becoming erratic and impulsive if more satisfying fare ever presented itself.<br /> <br /> A person in a situation to perform that moral calculus might deem that it's preferable for them to be satiated and relatively stable, at the cost of a somewhat small number of lives, than one that is constantly hungry and on edge and might be provoked into a terrible rampage.<br /> <br /> Still, the idea of being potentially benign is probably not enough to discount being creatures of darkness by itself. Like, some of the less harmful varieties of demon and probably a lot of ghosts fit that criteria and it's not enough to categorically exclude them, while there's still an option for individual good eggs to be excluded anyway.<br /> <br /> Actually, it's occurring to me... wasn't there some sense in Second Edition that shaped raksha weren't Creatures of Darkness primarily because in the era that the Unconquered Sun defended Creation there were hardly any of them and they were largely beneath his notice? I think by the standards of those books, there was also an answer of him not really being in a position to judge them as a threat and add them to the list, whether they warranted being there or not.<br /> <br /> I'm just thinking about that while I'm trying to assess questions of how to reconcile what the power of the Sun is and is not intrinsically anathema to when he's still supposed to have been once the direct guardian of the world. Mind, I suppose that could be resolved by him not exactly needing to inflict aggravated damage on everything he needs to fight off*, or just being able to invoke aggravated damage against everything he attacks by virtue of his sheer overwhelming might.<br /> <br /> Ultimately, it might be a bit of a moot point. You don't really need to have the light of the sun channelled through the strength of his Chosen by the thing to harm them in such fashion when an abundant mundane metal will typically do so.<br /> <br /> * Probably the biggest reason you don't need to inflict aggravated damage on the fae at all is if they don't exactly have much access to healing magic that would give it any distinction from lethal damage in the first place.</div> </div> </div> </div>Do Abyssals even need to drink people anymore to get Essence in Creation in 3e? Because that used to be an ironclad thing to emphasize how they have to spread shadowlands every which way to have an advantage.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-14T18:05:22-07:00","id":1540399,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1539675-the-raksha-not-enemies-of-the-sun?p=1540334#post1540334\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> And hungry ghosts are?</div> </div> </div> </div>Neverborn essence is anathema to the Sun just like Malfean essence is. As I recall, boring old human souls get a pass? But it seems like <i>monstrous</i> ghosts (hungry ghosts, nemissaries, nephracks, and so on) have taken on enough Essence of the Void to count.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/456-blackwell","name":"Blackwell","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar456_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"977"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-14T19:33:16-07:00","id":1540410,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Blackwell</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1539675-the-raksha-not-enemies-of-the-sun?p=1540399#post1540399\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Neverborn essence is anathema to the Sun just like Malfean essence is. As I recall, boring old human souls get a pass? But it seems like <i>monstrous</i> ghosts (hungry ghosts, nemissaries, nephracks, and so on) have taken on enough Essence of the Void to count.</div> </div> </div> </div>Or at least the Essence of where the sun doesn't shine.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-15T02:37:22-07:00","id":1540422,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Blackwell</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1539675-the-raksha-not-enemies-of-the-sun?p=1540399#post1540399\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Neverborn essence is anathema to the Sun just like Malfean essence is.</div> </div> </div> </div>But not the Essence of the world beyond Creation. Despite that being something the books still say he was originally charged with defending against, and which existed for unfathomable aeons before either Neverborn or Yozis?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Blackwell</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">As I recall, boring old human souls get a pass?</div> </div> </div> </div>It is stated in no uncertain terms that all undead count as creatures of darkness by default, and certain exceptions might be leveraged for particularly benevolent ones. The text for that found in Exalted: Essence has been quoted earlier in the thread, and the version in What Fire Has Wrought is hardly much different.<br /> <br /> I don't personally like making it much of a thing that it all ultimately extends back to the big Primordial originator, because I feel that takes too much focus away from the qualities of the beings themselves.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1539675-the-raksha-not-enemies-of-the-sun?p=1540398#post1540398\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Do Abyssals even need to drink people anymore to get Essence in Creation in 3e? Because that used to be an ironclad thing to emphasize how they have to spread shadowlands every which way to have an advantage.</div> </div> </div> </div>The draft manuscript references nothing exceptional about how Abyssals recover Essence one way or another.<br /> <br /> Abyssals outside of the Underworld or Shadowlands suffer a -2 penalty to all actions unless they adorn themselves in deathly trappings or while residing in a deathly themed place.<br /> <br /> They can build Limit by interacting with the living as though one of them (distinct from being perceived as one of the living for infiltration purposes). How onerous this is can vary, since Abyssals build Limit somewhat slowly and under more specific circumstances than other Celestial Exalted, but also expend it more gradually and can have the effects of their Curse be more unpleasant.<br /> <br /> I think that, all in all, Third Edition leans into the idea that being a combination of the living and the dead gives Abyssal Exalted somewhat more latitude than other denizens of the Underworld, and this is suitable to the desires of the Neverborn because being able to walk somewhat more freely in Creation allows them to evangelize the chivalry of the dead.<br /> <br /> A thing to keep in mind about Third Edition Abyssal Exalted is that while they are sworn to the death of Creation, the Neverborn don't want Creation to die quickly. Abyssals are not to kill people at will, they have to break down people's desire to live utterly before doing so. Abyssals are to preference the deaths of grandiose figures and great champions of life before moving on to the masses. Abyssals are to break down the boundaries between the living and the dead by encouraging intermingling of the two.<br /> <br /> Notably, the enforcement mechanism for the chivalry of death is more in the carrot than the stick. Abyssals aren't punished for failure to act on opportunities to carry it out (barring the Limit they gain if they should deliberately saves or spares lives in a manner inconsistent with mercy for the chivalry of death; curing a dying person so they can go on hurts, curing them because their torment is not yet at an end is A-OK), they're rewarded with Willpower and relief from their limit when they carry it out. Even then, given the scope of how they build Limit in the first place, a big part of the role of the Deathlords is to actually indoctrinate Abyssals in an ideology of the chivalry of death for its own sake. They've got to persuade their deathknights that all of this slow murder of the world is worthwhile and compelling, because the dark Lawgiver who goes their own way has a lot of latitude to just kind of not do that and live their best life as they can within the boundaries of the kinds of powers you can wield as that kind of Exalted.<br /> <br /> ... Actually, I suppose the strongest external incentive to carry out the chivalry of death actually would come to an Abyssal who was actively trying to avoid living up to the image by trying to be among the living, since they'll accumulate Limit at the highest rate. It puts them in a state of tension whereby their attempt to remain in the sunlit lands can only be safely maintained by constantly doing things that unsettle or distress the people around you.<br /> <br /> In that way, the incentive to create shadowlands isn't so much because it's where they can respire Essence as it is that it can potentially be a more benign way to keep their Curse from harming themselves or others. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-15T12:21:24-07:00","id":1540452,"title":"","content":"1e and 2e: Shadowlands as creeping plots of sheer doom, sucking Essence out of the world and weakening its heroes.<br /> <br /> 3e: Goth rave time! Go into the shadowland for a while and come out feeling like you can take on the world for another week!<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:8px\">(Pardon the flippant nature of the above, but it's kind of funny that you can re-frame it this way.)</span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-15T13:46:24-07:00","id":1540466,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1539675-the-raksha-not-enemies-of-the-sun?p=1540452#post1540452\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">1e and 2e: Shadowlands as creeping plots of sheer doom, sucking Essence out of the world and weakening its heroes.<br /> <br /> 3e: Goth rave time! Go into the shadowland for a while and come out feeling like you can take on the world for another week!<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:8px\">(Pardon the flippant nature of the above, but it's kind of funny that you can re-frame it this way.)</span></div> </div> </div> </div>Well, it's not as if shadowlands themselves are not less dangerous. Arguably more so, between the range of threatening Underworld residents we have and the revisions to how its geography works. An Abyssal who generates such a space for their own comfort is still being fairly cavalier with the wellbeing of living Creation around them.<br /> <br /> That's another facet to the tension that can hang over Abyssals; with proper management, being part of the living world is within the range of possibility, but given the risks and costs it might entail, whose benefit is it for?<br /> <br /> (On an unrelated note, Abyssals might not be directly punished for failure to adhere to the chivalry of death, but Deathlords very much are. An Abyssal who strays too far may incur the wrath of their liege driven by fear of the wrath of <i>their</i> liege.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-15T19:29:50-07:00","id":1540494,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1539675-the-raksha-not-enemies-of-the-sun?p=1540422#post1540422\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But not the Essence of the world beyond Creation. Despite that being something the books still say he was originally charged with defending against, and which existed for unfathomable aeons before either Neverborn or Yozis?</div> </div> </div> </div>I had a response and then realized a smart person already said it:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1539675-the-raksha-not-enemies-of-the-sun?p=1539689#post1539689\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think the main reason for the shift is that the original developers wanted to make it more about something that would literally be harmed by the cleansing light of the sun, rather than being on a list of enemies.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think that's consistent with a reversion past 2e, almost to 1e.<br /> <br /> The first formal definition of Creature of Darkness that I can find is 2e core which is when Demons and Unshaped were added. In 1e Core the first reference I can find the &quot;creatures of darkness&quot;, lower case, is in Melee and a family of Charms that have enhanced effects against &quot;creatures of the night, the walking dead, and Abyssal Exalted&quot;.<br /> <br /> I think 2e's definition was when we went to &quot;the sun's shitlist&quot;, where before the idea was more a metaphysical state of <i>dark</i> that make you vulnerable to the Sun's light. Mountain Folk's Cephalids and Buried Gods seem more naturally &quot;Creatures of Darkness&quot; than most species of demon. See also Five Days Darkness. Similarly early 1e's metaphysical opinion of Fair Folk seemed to be more &quot;Order resists Chaos&quot; or &quot;Order brings shape to Chaos&quot;, not &quot;Order <i>scourges</i> Chaos&quot;. <br /> <br /> All things considered I think my preferred definition of Creatures of Darkness would be &quot;Anything from the Underworld, plus individuals and species of gods, demons, and stranger things with particularly flee-from-sunlight resonance. The Sun doesn't have any animosity to these CoDs as a class, though he does have <i>specific</i> animosities toward many of them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/456-blackwell","name":"Blackwell","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar456_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"977"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}